# spectral/runs/: legacy A-N v17 run evidence, deliberately preserved as
# local historical evidence rather than committed canonical source (see
# spectral/legacy/v17/ on research/spectral-a-to-n-v18 for the immutable,
# hash-verified, committed copy).
spectral/runs/

# docs/research/truth_audit_2026_07_29/: earlier advisory (non-canonical)
# audit of CANONICAL_FINITE_CORE, kept as local reference material — not
# part of any registered claim/theorem evidence chain.
docs/research/truth_audit_2026_07_29/

# runs/: SEION-KGR v25/v26 trainer run artifacts (checkpoints, metrics,
# manifests). Same convention as artifacts/runs/** and spectral/runs/
# above — local evidence, not committed canonical source. Checkpoints in
# particular are large binaries that do not belong in git history.
runs/

# data/: knowledge-graph benchmark datasets (FB15K-237, WN18RR, CoDEx-M,
# DB100K+, YAGO3-10). Not committed — large third-party data, not
# repository source. Fetch/place locally before running seion_kgr_v26_train.py.
data/

# campaigns/*/tier*/ and campaigns/*/*_run/: individual run output
# directories (checkpoints, per-run manifests) from the Gate 12 campaign.
# Compact summaries, preregistration, and logs directly under
# campaigns/gate12/ ARE committed; per-run .pt checkpoints are not.
campaigns/*/*_run/
campaigns/*/tier*/
campaigns/*/screening/
campaigns/*/confirmatory/
